I am thrilled to share with you two papers I will present next week, based on our HAVI Schmidt Sciences "Recovering Hidden Histories - Adapting Handwritten Text Recognition for Colonial Paraguayan Archives". 
First, next Monday, June 15th, between 13:30 and 15:05 (Luxembourg time), I will participate remotely in the "AI through History, History through AI" in Panel II: Decolonizing AI and Marginalized Archives with [a paper titled](https://www.uni.lu/c2dh-en/events/ai-through-history-history-through-ai/#monday-15-june-2026) "Adapting AI for Marginalised Archives: Developing Handwritten Text Recognition Models for Colonial Paraguayan Manuscripts"
Second, next Tuesday, June 16th, between 9:30 and 11:00 AM (UK time), I will give, in person, [a paper titled](https://digitalhumanities-uk-ie.org/2026-annual-event-programme/) "Sustaining Hidden Histories: Adapting AI Technologies for Colonial Paraguayan Archives" in the UK-Ireland Digital Humanities Association - Sustainability 2026 Annual Event at the University of Southampton.
